⚡🇦🇺 A man spent 945 days in immigration detention in Australia because authorities misinterpreted the law, the Australian Broadcasting Corporation (ABC) reported, citing a Commonwealth Ombudsman report.

The man left Australia after his birth, but returned in 1992 and should have been automatically granted citizenship upon turning 10. However, in 2022 his presence in the country was recognized as unlawful. Authorities managed to determine his citizenship only after a fourth assessment. According to the report, this is not an isolated case.

